  "adaptations": [
    "This is a live native adaptation of the supplied 1586 by 992 concept, not a claimed pixel-identical replica. Current parameter values and selected states are not baked into the artwork.",
    "The XY pad controls the real Macro 1 and Macro 2 parameters. The two axes and adjacent knobs stay synchronized; this is not a general scene timbre morph engine.",
    "The concept's Scene Morph slider is replaced by a correctly labeled selected-scene level control and the actual constrained filter-routing menu. Scene mode and voice mode use the existing native parameters.",
    "All eight macros remain available, flanking the central XY pad. Their labels identify real macros rather than promising the concept's unassigned Drive, Color or Evolve destinations.",
    "The three oscillator cards are independent real oscillator editors. Unsupported generic Sample labels and fictitious oscillator tuning readouts are not reproduced.",
    "The lower keyboard is a playable native MIDI keyboard. Six performance snapshots, three independent key zones, expression and touch lanes from the concept are not falsely displayed as implemented features. The actual two-scene split point, voice limit, glide, width, pan and tuning remain available.",
    "Four narrow performance faders follow the reference's physical lane placement but remain explicitly labeled Octave, Glide, Width and Pan, controlling those real parameters. They do not pretend to implement pitch-wheel, expression or touch lanes.",
    "The visible envelope uses the actual amplitude envelope and the two LFO previews use their own native LFOs. The other envelope and all remaining modulators remain accessible through Full editor.",
    "Eight visible effect-type selectors control actual slots. All sixteen effect slots and detailed effect controls are available through Full FX editor.",
    "The upper center uses a perspective stack of the actual oscillator preview. The output panel uses real signal levels and exposes Open scope for detailed native analysis rather than inventing a spectrogram.",
    "The shared header retains native preset navigation, scene selection, skin selection and Full editor access. Unsupported snapshot and analyzer mode tabs are not decorative pretend buttons."
  ]
}
